+## List-renormalised PIP fields (additive output, HQ order 2026-11-17; spec `SPEC_LIST_PIP.md`)
+
+`v3_fit` additionally returns `pip_list` (named like `pip_primary`), `mpm_list`, `log_Z_list`, `list_size`, `list_full`, `pip_list_source` (`"store"` or `"exact"`) and `pip_list_flag` (absent when clean; `"empty_list"` or `"nonfinite_score"` with NA fields): the posterior renormalised to the returned top store `top_store` (the store's scores F(S), subtracted by their maximum before `exp`; both sums run from the last store entry to the first, in plain double). `pip_primary` and `mpm` stay the primary outputs; nothing else changes, no random number is read, and the fields are computed last (`v3_list_fields` in `v3_run.R`). Exact branch: `pip_list = pip_primary`, `mpm_list = mpm`, `log_Z_list` from the enumeration's returned store (`fit$exact$top`). Every other status (resource limit, invalid input, no predictors, constant response, numerical failure, calibration stop): the fields are absent. Tests: `../tests/list_pip_units.R`.
+
+Two readings of the spec are Theory-confirmed (via HQ 2026-11-17). (1) Exact branch (status `exact`): `pip_list = pip_primary` (the enumeration PIPs), `mpm_list = mpm`, `log_Z_list` from the store `fit$exact$top`, `list_size` / `list_full` describe that same store, `pip_list_source = "exact"`. (2) A score of −Inf gets weight 0; if ALL scores are −Inf (normaliser 0) the fields are NA and `pip_list_flag = "nonfinite_score"` (the NaN / +Inf rule extended to 0/0).
+
+Order of computation: `v3_fit` adds the list fields strictly LAST, after `finish()` has sampled `peak_memory_kb`, the clock and the runtime guard, so they cannot touch a legacy field; direct callers of `v3_final_run` get them by default (`list_fields = TRUE`; `v3_fit` passes FALSE and adds them itself). Error precedence: an empty list is flagged, then a duplicate model stops, then a non-finite score flags; a flagged result is all NA (`mpm_list = NA_integer_`).
